{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_widen_1.march","start_line":23,"start_col":16,"end_line":23,"end_col":31,"message":"`widen` takes a `Cap(IO.Console)` parameter, but capability values were retired: a function no longer receives its authority, it uses the current authority, which `main`'s `needs` clause asks for and each operation checks.\nhelp: remove the parameter and the argument at each call; to state what `widen` may use, give it a `needs` clause.","code":"cap_param_retired","fix":{"kind":"multi","edits":[{"kind":"replace","start_line":23,"start_col":12,"end_line":23,"end_col":31,"text":""}],"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"},"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_widen_1.march","start_line":23,"start_col":35,"end_line":23,"end_col":52,"message":"`Cap(IO.FileWrite)` was retired: capability values grant nothing since the current authority replaced them.\nhelp: remove it; code uses the current authority, which `main`'s `needs` clause asks for and each operation checks.","code":"cap_param_retired","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_widen_1.march","start_line":24,"start_col":4,"end_line":24,"end_col":17,"message":"`Cap(IO.Console)` cannot be widened to `Cap(IO.FileWrite)` — `cap_narrow` only attenuates, so the source capability must subsume the target.\nhelp: `Cap(IO.FileWrite)` is not below `Cap(IO.Console)` in the capability lattice. Receive it from a caller that holds an ancestor of it.","code":"cap_widen","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_widen_1.march","start_line":24,"start_col":4,"end_line":24,"end_col":17,"message":"`cap_narrow` was retired with the capability values it narrowed.\nhelp: remove the call; to run code under less authority, use `restrict SCOPE do ... end`.","code":"cap_narrow_retired","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
{"severity":"warning","file":"errors/cap_widen_1.march","start_line":27,"start_col":16,"end_line":27,"end_col":23,"message":"`main` asks for its authority with `Cap` parameters, which are deprecated and will be removed in the next release: a capability value grants nothing since the current authority replaced it.\nhelp: request it with a `needs` clause: `fn main() needs IO do`.","code":"deprecated_main_cap","fix":{"kind":"multi","edits":[{"kind":"replace","start_line":27,"start_col":9,"end_line":27,"end_col":24,"text":"()"},{"kind":"replace","start_line":27,"start_col":25,"end_line":27,"end_col":25,"text":"needs IO "}],"applicability":"machine-applicable"},"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
